CORE
main.py
--unwind 3

^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[python-unbound-local\.\d+\] .*local variable 'x' referenced before assignment \(UnboundLocalError\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
differential2 §12b cross-branch (now detected). x is assigned only on
the c=True branch, so f(False) raises UnboundLocalError. A runtime
is-bound flag per plain-Assign local -- false at entry, set true after
the binding statement at the convert_statement chokepoint (keyed on the
AST target, independent of how the value write was built), asserted at
each read -- makes this path-sensitive, so the c=False path is caught.

